meta-qti-eap
============

This layer provides packages and a kernel add-on package to enable connecting
an AP (applications processor) to a QTI modem system. The connection can be
done via PCIe or USB.

The Telematics SDK is included to facilitate creating applications that
communicate with the modem to perform various actions and get notified about
state changes. Some examples are: starting a voice call, sending an SMS,
starting CV2X mode, etc.

A default telematics-image is provided for initial verification of the system.
It is based on the core-image-minimal image with utilities and QTI packages
added to it.

Dependencies
------------

This layer depends on:

  git://git.openembedded.org/openembedded-core
  git://git.yoctoproject.org/meta-yocto
  git://git.openembedded.org/meta-openembedded

Adding the meta-qti-eap layer to your build
-------------------------------------------

In order to use this layer, you need to make the build system aware of
it.

Assuming the meta-qti-eap layer exists at the top-level of your
yocto build tree, you can add it to the build system by adding the
location of the meta-qti-eap layer to bblayers.conf, along with any
other layers needed. e.g.:

  BBLAYERS += "/path/to/root/sources/meta-qti-eap"

Making a build
--------------

Example using the qemuarm64 machine. First source the environment script:

$ source sources/meta-qti-eap/scripts/set_env_bb.sh

This will create the build folder and move to it. Now start the build:

$ MACHINE=qemuarm64 bitbake telematics-image

